Pill Engine - Licensing
=======================

Copyright (c) Mateusz Szymoński and the Pill Engine contributors.

Pill Engine is free for everyone who builds with it, from a solo developer
to a large studio, and it grows through what its community gives back. It
is offered under three alternative licensing routes. Choose the one that
fits you; you need only one, and the conditions of one never apply to
someone using another, except obligations already taken on under it.
Commercial use is allowed under all three. Using Pill Engine without
choosing another licensing route means accepting the Community License. A
"User Project" is anything built with Pill Engine: a game, simulation,
visualization or other application.

1. Community License - legal/licenses/COMMUNITY_LICENSE.md
   Free for everyone, for commercial User Projects too, and your own code
   always stays private. Your changes to the engine (Pill Engine
   Modifications) may stay private below USD 300,000 Annual Revenue; once you
   grow past it, you are required to share them with the community within
   3 months, or switch to the Open Source licensing route or a Partner
   License. No forks or standalone engines without permission.
   Source-available, not OSI-approved open source.

2. Open Source License - legal/licenses/EUPL-1.2_LICENSE.txt
   SPDX-License-Identifier: EUPL-1.2
   Free for everyone, with no revenue limit, for proprietary User Projects
   too. When you distribute a User Project or make it available over a
   network, you must make the source code of the Pill Engine version it
   contains available under the EUPL-1.2. For an unchanged Pill Engine, a
   link to the official repository is enough; if you changed it, publish
   your version with your Pill Engine Modifications, for example as a
   public fork. Your User Code stays private, as the Licensor's statement
   in that file confirms.

3. Partner License - legal/licenses/PARTNER_LICENSE.md
   A paid agreement with the Licensor for keeping Pill Engine
   Modifications private at any revenue, without the Community License's
   publishing duty, for the code it covers. Partner funding is meant to
   support the further development of Pill Engine, giving both partners and
   the community a stronger engine to build on, while keeping it free for
   everyone. In the future, it will go to a non-profit foundation for Pill
   Engine, independent of any company, once that foundation exists (see
   legal/GOVERNANCE.md). The Partner License is always a choice, never a
   requirement, includes no support or maintenance unless the agreement says
   otherwise, and exists only once signed by both parties.

Third-party components keep their own licenses (see
legal/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md), which none of these licensing routes
overrides.

This file is only a summary. If it differs from the full text of the license
you choose, the full text applies.
